    icon: '🃏',
  },
  data: {
    LLM: "1. **Lead Tile**: One player reveals the rightmost domino in their line and announces its two suits (or single suit if a double). 2. **Other Players' Turns**: Each other player, in turn, reveals their rightmost domino. 3. **Trick Winner**: The player whose revealed domino matches one of the two suits from the lead tile wins all face-up dominoes (the 'trick'). 4. **Captured Tiles**: The trick winner places captured dominoes at the left end of their line, face-down. 5. **Next Round**: The trick winner leads the next round by revealing their new rightmost domino. 6. **Elimination**: Players who run out of dominoes exit the game. 7. **Game End**: The last remaining player with dominoes wins.",
    Player: "1. **Lead Tile**: One player reveals the rightmost domino in their line and announces its two suits (or single suit if a double). 2. **Other Players' Turns**: Each other player, in turn, reveals their rightmost domino. 3. **Trick Winner**: The player whose revealed domino matches one of the two suits from the lead tile wins all face-up dominoes (the 'trick'). 4. **Captured Tiles**: The trick winner places captured dominoes at the left end of their line, face-down. 5. **Next Round**: The trick winner leads the next round by revealing their new rightmost domino. 6. **Elimination**: Players who run out of dominoes exit the game. 7. **Game End**: The last remaining player with dominoes wins.",
    objective: 'Be the first player to accumulate all dominoes by winning tricks.',
    gameplay: "1. **Lead Tile**: One player reveals the rightmost domino in their line and announces its two suits (or single suit if a double). 2. **Other Players' Turns**: Each other player, in turn, reveals their rightmost domino. 3. **Trick Winner**: The player whose revealed domino matches one of the two suits from the lead tile wins all face-up dominoes (the 'trick'). 4. **Captured Tiles**: The trick winner places captured dominoes at the left end of their line, face-down. 5. **Next Round**: The trick winner leads the next round by revealing their new rightmost domino. 6. **Elimination**: Players who run out of dominoes exit the game. 7. **Game End**: The last remaining player with dominoes wins.",
    keyRules: [
      'Dominoes must be arranged face-down in a single horizontal line.',
      'Players always reveal from the rightmost position in their line.',
      'To win a trick, a domino must match one (or both) suits of the lead tile.',
      'Captured dominoes are placed at the left of the line, face-down.',
      'The trick winner always leads the next round.',
      'Players eliminated when they have no dominoes left.',
      'Extras not distributed during dealing are removed from play entirely.',
