      "Turn-flow example: 1. **Lead Tile**: One player reveals the rightmost domino in their line and announces its two suits (or single suit if a double). 2. **Other Players' Turns**: Each other player, in turn, reveals their rightmost domino. 3. **Trick Winner**: The player whose revealed domino matches one of the two suits from the lead tile wins all face-up dominoes (the 'trick'). 4. **Captured Tiles**: The trick winner places captured dominoes at the left end of their line, face-down. 5. **Next Round**: The trick winner leads the next round by revealing their new rightmost domino. 6. **Elimination**: Players who run out of dominoes exit the game. 7. **Game End**: The last remaining player with dominoes wins.",
